;; What this case exercises; edit by hand.  `bb corpus-accept' leaves it alone.
(:book "empirical analysis of programming language popularity"
 :source "empirical analysis of programming language popularity.pdf"
 :page 2
 :exercises "Org emphasis from the font runs: the run-in bold lead kept
in its paragraph as *...*, italic phrases as /.../, a bold-italic
name nested /*...*/, an italic phrase the wrap split bridged whole
((/MOOC all/)), the enumerator left outside its item's markers, and
the bold section heads (2. Methodology, 2.1 Data) as org headings
with no markers.  The glued budget is this page's stable camel-case
proper nouns (SourceForge x4, GitHub, MacIver, SaaS x2), the OCR
measure's known cost on brand-name prose."
 :budget (:mid-sentence 0 :glued 8))
